# Every file that ships is byte-identical on every platform.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf decides line endings per machine: the repository
# stores LF, a Windows checkout receives CRLF, and `git archive` hands out CRLF
# too. A package built from a working tree that kept LF then differs from one
# built from a fresh clone, by one byte per line in every text file that ships.
#
# AMO rebuilds the source it is given and compares it against the uploaded
# package. That difference is the whole gap between a reproducible build and a
# rejected submission. Found on 2.7.0: three _locales/*/messages.json files, six
# bytes each.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, untouched.
*.png binary
*.zip binary
*.ico binary
